# OpenFGA (`openfga-openfga`)

OpenFGA is an authorization and permission engine inspired by Google Zanzibar that lets you model and enforce fine-grained access control in your applications. It exposes developer-friendly HTTP and gRPC APIs for writing authorization models, storing relationship tuples, and performing authorization checks, with SDKs available for common languages. OpenFGA supports multiple storage backends, including PostgreSQL, MySQL, and SQLite (beta), so you can choose the persistence layer that fits your environment.

With Eyevinn Open Source Cloud (OSC), you can consume OpenFGA as a managed service instead of running and operating it yourself. That means no servers to provision, no Docker Compose stacks to maintain, and no time spent on configuring and tuning a production deployment just to get started. You get an OpenFGA endpoint ready to use, and it fits into the rest of OSC so you can provision and manage it alongside your other open source managed services.

[Source](https://github.com/openfga/openfga)

## Example

```terraform
resource "osc_instance" "example" {
  service_id = "openfga-openfga"
  name       = "myopenfga"

  sensitive_parameters = {
    DatabaseUrl = var.database_url
    PresharedKey = var.preshared_key
  }
}
```

Commented lines are optional parameters. Values marked `"..."` need a real value. Outputs are `url`, `external_ip`, `external_port` and the raw `instance` document, see the `osc_instance` resource.

## Parameters

| Name | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `DatabaseUrl` | string | yes | PostgreSQL connection URL for OpenFGA's datastore, for example postgres://user:password@host:5432/dbname. The database schema is created and migrated automatically on every start. Feeds OPENFGA_DATASTORE_URI. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |
| `PresharedKey` | string | yes | API key that every client must send as an Authorization: Bearer header. Without a valid key all API calls are rejected with 401; only /healthz needs no key. Keep it secret and set it in your apps as well. Feeds OPENFGA_AUTHN_PRESHARED_KEYS. Sensitive, set it in `sensitive_parameters`. |

The instance `name` must match `^\w+$` and be unique per service within the workspace. OSC lowercases it and allows at most 20 characters.

Parameter values are strings; booleans take `"true"` or `"false"`. Reference an `osc_secret` as `osc_secret.<name>.ref` to keep a value out of the instance configuration. This page is generated from the OSC catalog; the provider validates against the live catalog when planning.
